# Git hygiene

- Do **not** assume intent for git actions. If staging, committing, pushing, branching, or resetting is unclear, **ask first**.
- Do **not** stage files (`git add`, `git restore --staged`, index updates). Leave the working tree unstaged so I can review before staging.
- Do **not** commit unless I explicitly instruct you to commit.
- Updating or creating files in the working tree is fine; git index and history changes require my say-so.

```text
# ❌ BAD — agent stages after editing
git add README.md app/models/url_mapping.rb

# ✅ GOOD — edit files, leave staging to the user
# (no git add / commit unless asked)
```
